  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1954-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For \\(x\\ne0,\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} &1+\\left(\\frac{x^4-1}{2x^2}\\right)^2\\\\ &\\quad=\\frac{4x^4+(x^4-1)^2}{4x^4}\\\\ &\\quad=\\frac{(x^4+1)^2}{4x^4}. \\end{aligned} \\] Because \\(x^2\\gt0,\\) its square root is \\[ \\frac{x^4+1}{2x^2} =\\frac{x^2}{2}+\\frac1{2x^2}. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Put \\(1\\) over the denominator \\(4x^4\\)",
        "The numerator becomes \\(4x^4+(x^4-1)^2=(x^4+1)^2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
